A significant challenge of managing a complicated project is the sheer breadth and depth of technical detail. Often, program managers must have enough mastery of detail to facilitate meaningful conversations with customers, sales teams, engineers and other domain experts even though they likely have less domain-specific knowledge than those with whom they are interacting. This presents a challenge, as it means that technical program managers are constantly having to navigate new technologies or use cases, and learning how things work on their own.  What’s an example of something that you needed to explore, reverse engineer, decipher, or otherwise figure out as part of a program or project and how did you do it? What impact did this have on customer or other key stakeholder engagement? Please provide as much detail as you can recall.



